# Architecture Enforcement

**Authoritative source:** `docs/architecture.md`. This rule only enforces it.

If implementation conflicts with `docs/architecture.md`, change the implementation—not the architecture (or supersede via ADR).

Consult by section: §2 Principles · §4 Layers · §5 Dependency Rule · §6–7 Folders · §9 Responsibilities · §10 Repositories · §12 DB access · §14 Validation · §16–17 Checklists · §18 Placement.

## Must follow

- Consult `docs/architecture.md` before introducing new layers, modules, or architectural abstractions.
- When unsure where new code belongs, use the placement guidance in §18 instead of guessing.
- Obey the Dependency Rule (§2.2, §5): dependencies point inward; Domain depends on nothing outer.
- Place code by layer ownership (§4, §9, §18): Presentation / Application / Domain / Infrastructure.
- Keep business logic out of Presentation (§4.1, §9).
- Keep framework and infrastructure types out of Domain (§4.3, §5).
- Access Supabase and provider SDKs only in Infrastructure (§4.4, §12).
- Depend on repository/query interfaces—never concrete adapters—from Application (§10, §11).
- Segregate command repos from query interfaces; do not mix in one fat port (§2.12, §10).
- Map persistence rows before leaving Infrastructure; never return raw persistence models (§10).
- Respect feature boundaries: no cross-feature `infrastructure/` imports (§6–7).
- Wire concretes only in feature `composition.ts` / composition root (§7, §11).

## Hard reject

- Dependency Rule violation (e.g. Domain → Application/Infrastructure; Presentation → Infrastructure).
- Business logic in controllers, routes, or Zod schemas.
- Domain importing Express, Supabase, Pino, env, or any provider SDK.
- Supabase/SQL (or `.from(...)`) outside Infrastructure.
- Use case importing a concrete repository/adapter class or SDK types.
- Bypassing repository/query ports (direct DB/SDK from Application/Presentation).
- Returning unmapped persistence rows or table-shaped types across boundaries.
- Cross-feature infrastructure coupling.
- Anemic Domain (invalid-state VOs; entities as data bags with no invariants).
- Duplicating a Domain VO rule in Zod instead of delegating (§14).
- Creating new architectural patterns, abstractions, or dependency directions that contradict `docs/architecture.md` without an approved ADR.

## Review checklist

- ✓ Correct layer ownership (§4, §9, §18)
- ✓ Dependency direction respected (§5)
- ✓ Repository/query interfaces used (§10)
- ✓ No framework leakage into Domain (§4.3, §5)
- ✓ DTOs at boundaries (§4.2, §9)
- ✓ Business rules in Domain/Application (§4.2–4.3)
- ✓ Persistence only in Infrastructure (§4.4, §12)
- ✓ No deviation from `docs/architecture.md` without an ADR

When this rule and `docs/architecture.md` appear to differ, treat `docs/architecture.md` as authoritative. Do not invent or infer architecture beyond what it specifies.
